<h2>Prerequisites</h2>
<ul>
    <li>You are <a href="../../login">logged in</a>.</li>
    <li>You have <a href="how-to-enable-creator-and-use-modules">activated Creator mode</a>.</li>
</ul>
<h1>How to install the plugin</h1>
<p>First of all, download the latest version of the plugin <a href="">here</a></p>
<p>Move the plugin file to your server plugins folder.<br>After doing so you should start your server so the plugin will
    generate the nessecary files.</p>
<h2>Configuring the plugin</h2>
<p>After the plugin has created the nessecary files, navigate to your <b>plugins</b> folder, and the
    <b>StreamerOptions</b> folder within. <br>Here you will find a <b>config.yml</b> file that we will edit.
</p>
<img src="../../i/g/minecraft_plugin_setup/img0.png" alt="The default configuration">
<p>First of all, you will need to change the <b>token</b> value to the token you can find on your Creator dashboard.</p>
<img src="../../i/g/minecraft_plugin_setup/img1.png" alt="The token">
<p>After doing so, you need to add the UUID's of the players the plugin will have effect on in the config, or add the
    players via commands. <br>To do so using commands, simply use
    <b>/streamer add playername</b> in the Minecraft chat. To remove a streamer use <b>/streamer remove
        playername</b>.<br>If you want to see which players are currenyly added, use <b>/streamer list</b>.<br><br>For
    adding in config, you can
    get UUID's by using a website like <a href="https://namemc.com">namemc</a>.<br>If you want to add multiple players,
    make sure to remove the # before the line, or else it will be a comment.
</p>
<p>If you are planning on using the whitelist module, we strongly suggest to disable announcing who was whitelisted.<br>
    This can be anything a viewer wants, and be abused to say bad things. By default, this isn't disabled.</p>
<h4>You should now be able to use the Streamer Options Minecraft plugin and its modules.</h4>